# Understand-Anything exclusions for ForgeOps.
#
# Layered on top of the tool's DEFAULT_IGNORE_PATTERNS (node_modules/, .git/, .venv/,
# dist/, *.lock, binaries, …). Everything here is either not source, not ours, or must
# never be read into an analysis index.
#
# The order of these sections mirrors the reason each entry exists.

# --- Must never be read. Non-negotiable. ------------------------------------
# `.env` holds real local credentials. `.env.example` is placeholder-only by contract
# and is deliberately NOT excluded: it is part of the configuration surface a reader
# needs to understand.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
credentials.json

# --- Not ours. ---------------------------------------------------------------
backend/.venv/
frontend/node_modules/
agent/dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Not source: scratch, evidence capture and one-off probes. ---------------
# `.evidence/` is a working capture directory, and `scripts/_*` are diagnostic
# one-offs. Both would swamp the graph with nodes nobody navigates.
.evidence/
scripts/_*
*.tmp
.commitmsg.tmp

# --- Vendored or generated artifacts that carry no design intent. ------------
agent/testfixtures/
backend/alembic/script.py.mako
frontend/public/
